# Deploy and refresh (agent-owned)

The user does **not** run deploy/build scripts. After meaningful API or web changes, the agent must:

## Contabo VPS (production)

Run without asking the user:

```powershell
cd c:\Users\pj\WizCRM
git add -A && git commit && git push origin development   # when there are changes
.\scripts\deploy-vps.ps1 -SkipPush   # after push; or full deploy-vps.ps1 if already pushed
```

Or SSH equivalent: `scripts/deploy-vps.sh` on the server (`git pull`, `npm run build -w shared`, `api` prisma db push + build, `VITE_API_URL=https://api.wizcrm.app npm run web:build`, copy `web/dist` → `/var/www/wizcrm-web`, `systemctl restart wizcrm-api`, reload caddy).

## Local workspace

After web/API edits, run `.\scripts\refresh-local.ps1` (or the same build steps). Restart `npm run web:dev` in background if it was running so the user can refresh the browser only.

## User role

User checks whether https://api.wizcrm.app, https://app.wizcrm.app (when DNS exists), and local http://localhost:5180 work — no manual script execution.
